-A processing failure does not become a completion verdict.
+`pending → running → reviewed`; transient judge/schema/transport failures preserve pending work and a retry wake. Every turn's final output and attempted stop are buffered before external delivery or terminal Runs/child publication. Streaming status/tool activity may continue, but unreviewed handoff/final text cannot leak. A stop approved as unnecessary is silently replaced by continuation. Ordinary final outputs that finish the request pass through once.
 
 ### 8.2 Verdict definitions
 
-| Verdict | Exact meaning |
-|---|---|
-| `complete` | All mandatory current criteria pass; semantic coverage passes; hard constraints pass; no unknown effects remain; no required child remains unfinished. |
-| `continue` | Useful authorized work remains executable now within the current scope and budget. |
-| `waiting` | The objective remains open, but a dependency or scheduled time prevents useful immediate execution. A durable wake exists. |
-| `blocked` | Progress requires a real missing decision, identity interaction, denied permission, unavailable capability without a safe alternative, or explicit pause. |
-| `failed` | The execution failed to achieve an outcome and needs recovery or repair. The underlying obligation remains open. |
