+### 10.3 Automatic ship and feedback
 
-Development failures follow [TEST-PLAN's P7 correction flow](TEST-PLAN.md#correction-ladder-for-development-failures-p7): make recurrence impossible through architecture/types/data constraints, then add static enforcement, then guidance for any justified remainder; human style review is never the sole fix. Extend an existing largest-interface case when it reaches the defect, and reject repeated systematic failures closed with memory-only guidance.
+On passing exact-artifact evaluation, protected publisher auto-ships and Attention emits one `Fixed: …` line. Same-cause complaint immediately rolls compatible code back, preserving newer obligations, receipts and permanent tests; next fix needs a stronger P7 rung (or stronger structural invariant at rung 1). Start ordinary repairs immediately in the background while current work uses an authorized workaround. Only huge rebuilds use the single nightly phase. Weekly cause-specific frustration trends that are flat/rising open a System 2 incident.
 
