+The C/B/I support/behavior/infrastructure hierarchy remains acyclic: a top-level disposable I experiment may drive one repair; child C/B judgments do not spawn recursive repairs. `toy_si.experiment` remains evaluator-owned and `$TOY_ROOT/control/publisher.db` alone owns real publication. Synthetic I uses separate test release/control stores, never a production pointer. P7 structural/static prevention comes first, justified behavioral guidance is allowed on replay pass, permission/Authority rules and spending never change. Full CLI/P5/feature-map evidence is required.
 
